const BLUEPRINT_DATA = [{"title": "Robot Extension", "category": "Miscellaneous", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/robo_extension.webp", "desc": "<p>Easily extend your robot network with this blueprint. It snaps to a 50x50 grid so it&#x27;s very easy to correctly tile these. Some of my other blueprints below are designed to fit inside of it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "1 Roboport", "string": ""}, {"label": "3x3", "string": ""}, {"label": "5x5", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Solar Panel Block", "category": "Power", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/solar_block.webp", "desc": "<p>A tileable solar panel block that perfectly fits overtop of the robot extension blueprint. The ratio is as close to the ideal .84 as possible without wasting space.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Solar Panel Block with Walkway", "category": "Power", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/solar_block_walkway.webp", "desc": "<p>This one has a built-in walkway (or, driveway, I suppose). Is it useful? I don&#x27;t know. But one thing I do know: it exists!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Nuclear Power", "category": "Power", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/nuclear_power.webp", "desc": "<p>This can generate up to 480MW and won&#x27;t waste fuel. You can place one fuel cell in the bottom right reactor to start it up (or one in each should be fine, too). More fuel cells will only be added when the stored power gets low enough. You&#x27;ll have to pipe in a bunch of water, of course, but, hey, water is cheap.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Fusion Power (400MW)", "category": "Power", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/fusion_power_400.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;ll need to kick start this with a bit of fluoroketone, but once you&#x27;re done that it&#x27;ll hum along just fine!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Fusion Power (1.2GW)", "category": "Power", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/fusion_power_1200.webp", "desc": "<p>MOAR POWER!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Mining", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/mining.webp", "desc": "<p>A bunch of different-sized mining blueprints I find useful. One of these should cover just about any mining field.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "30x4 Miners, Yellow Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "30x5 Miners, Red Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "30x6 Miners, Red Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "30x7 Miners, Red Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "30x8 Miners, Red Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "60x4 Miners, Red Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "60x5 Miners, Red Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "60x6 Miners, Red Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "60x7 Miners, Red Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "60x8 Miners, Red Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "60x5 Miners, Blue Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "60x6 Miners, Blue Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "60x7 Miners, Blue Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "60x8 Miners, Blue Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Stone Smelter Line", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/stone_smelters.webp", "desc": "<p>These will smelt a full yellow belt and can be easily tiled vertically. You can choose between the coal line going up, going down, or being fed by a box (for very early game). You can also choose between input and output being on the same side or different sides.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Coal from above, output/input opposite sides", "string": ""}, {"label": "Coal from above, output/input same side", "string": ""}, {"label": "Coal from below, output/input opposite sides", "string": ""}, {"label": "Coal from below, output/input same side", "string": ""}, {"label": "Box-fed coal, output/input opposite sides", "string": ""}, {"label": "Box-fed coal, output/input same side", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Steel Smelter Line", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/steel_smelters.webp", "desc": "<p>Just like the stone smelter lines but steeler and morerer and redererer.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Coal from above, output/input opposite sides", "string": ""}, {"label": "Coal from above, output/input same side", "string": ""}, {"label": "Coal from below, output/input opposite sides", "string": ""}, {"label": "Coal from below, output/input same side", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Electric Smelter Line", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/electric_smelters.webp", "desc": "<p>Smelts a full yellow, red, or blue belt using electric furnaces, with the option to have the input on the same side or opposite sides.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Yellow belt, output/input opposite sides", "string": ""}, {"label": "Yellow belt, output/input same side", "string": ""}, {"label": "Red belt, output/input opposite sides", "string": ""}, {"label": "Red belt, output/input same side", "string": ""}, {"label": "Blue belt, output/input opposite sides", "string": ""}, {"label": "Blue belt, output/input same side", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Basic Oil Processing", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/basic_oil.webp", "desc": "<p>This will do basic oil processing. It&#x27;s a bit weird space-wise because it&#x27;s designed to be upgraded to the &quot;Advanced Oil Processing&quot; blueprint below.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Advanced Oil Processing", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/advanced_oil.webp", "desc": "<p>This output petroleum, light oil, and lubricant. If the lubricant backs up then so will the heavy oil, and if the heavy oil backs up the excess will be sent to light oil cracking. Likewise, the light oil backs up, it will be converted to petroleum. If the petroleum backs up--well then you&#x27;re in good shape, eh?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Coal Liquefaction", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/liquefaction.webp", "desc": "<p>Make that coal into precious oil! Ouputs petroleum, light oil, and lubricant. You&#x27;ll need to kick start the steam producing with a few pieces of coal or solid fuel. You&#x27;ll also have the kick start the heavy oil with a few barrels--you can dump them into the assembling machine and, once everything is going, you can remove the assembling machine.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Solid Fuel", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/solid_fuel.webp", "desc": "<p>This might look like an odd number of chemical plants (21), but that&#x27;s because it&#x27;s designed to completely consume light oil from the advanced oil blueprint.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Rocket Fuel", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/rocket_fuel.webp", "desc": "<p>Rocket fuel. Similar to the solid fuel, this is designed to fully-consume the light oil output of the advanced oil processing blueprint.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "AM2 Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Uranium Processing", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/uranium_processing.webp", "desc": "<p>Consumes either a yellow, red, or blue belt of uranium ore and outputs uranium-235 and uranium-238.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Through Yellow Belt", "string": ""}, {"label": "In-Out Yellow Belt", "string": ""}, {"label": "Through Red Belt", "string": ""}, {"label": "In-Out Red Belt", "string": ""}, {"label": "Through Blue Belt", "string": ""}, {"label": "In-Out Blue Belt", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Kovarex Enrichment", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/kovarex_1.webp", "desc": "<p>I hate this blueprint. It works almost by accident and it doesn&#x27;t scale up well. But even though I hate it, you should probably use it first before the other one below. It does a surprisingly good job of getting Kovarex enrichment going without too much waste. But as you expand it some of the centrifuges will end up needing to get to 80 uranium-235 in waiting before they start outputting.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Kovarex Enrichment", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/kovarex_2.webp", "desc": "<p>This is better than the other kovarex enchriment blueprint. It&#x27;s compact, efficient, and can tile forever. You could also beacon it easily (But don&#x27;t put productivity modules in! They won&#x27;t work!). BUT you have to manually feed in the first 40 uranium-235 to every centrifuge. So the other blueprint might be better to use early as it&#x27;s a bit more set-it-and-forget-it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Nuclear Fuel", "category": "Resources", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/nuclear_fuel.webp", "desc": "<p>This will consume all of the output of the &quot;Rocket Fuel&quot; blueprint and convert it into nuclear fuel ... assuming you can provide the uranium-235!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Train! (Solid Cargo)", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_car_solid.webp", "desc": "<p>This train car blueprint, if used with my other train blueprints below, will automatically pickup and dropoff any item and refuel itself at the refuel station. Just slap it down, put in enough fuel for it to get to the fuel station, and watch it go!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Train! (Liquid Cargo)", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_car_liquid.webp", "desc": "<p>Like the magic solid cargo train, this blueprint will automatically pickup and drop off any liquid items if used with my other blueprints.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Train Idle Area", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_idle_area.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;ll need at least one of these idle areas somewhere on your tracks for the magic trains to work. Magic trains will go here when they have no other work to do. You can infinitely expand it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Initial station", "string": ""}, {"label": "Expansion", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Train Refuel Station", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_refuel.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;ll need at least one of these refuel stations somewhere on your tracks for the magic trains to work. Magic trains will refuel themselves here. This can be used with either the single-train stop or multi-train stop blueprints farther below. When you put down the blueprint, it will ask you to select the fuel type for your trains (the stop will automatically remove other types of fuel from trains, so you can easily upgrade it and all your trains will eventually get faster). The blueprint book has two versions of the station, one is for early game and you have to supply the fuel yourself or belt it in, the other is for once you get requestor and active provider chests and the robots can supply the fuel instead.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint book", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Trains Solid Pickup", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_solid_pickup.webp", "desc": "<p>Magic trains will automatically pick up items from this station. This is designed to work with the station blueprints farther below. The &quot;w/priority&quot; versions will automatically set the station priority based on how much is available to pick up.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint book", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Trains Solid Dropoff", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_solid_dropoff.webp", "desc": "<p>Magic trains will automatically drop off items at this station. When you place the blueprint down, it will ask you to select what type of item should be dropped off. Once it&#x27;s down, the trains will start coming all by themselves! The output is belt- and lane-balanced so you can feed it directly to a bus.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint book", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Trains Liquid Pickup", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_liquid_pickup.webp", "desc": "<p>Magic trains will automatically pickup up liquid from this station.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint book", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Trains Liquid Dropoff", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_liquid_dropoff.webp", "desc": "<p>Magic trains will automatically drop off liquid at this station. When you place the blueprint down, it will ask you to select what type of liquid should be dropped off.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint book", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Trains Solid Pickup (depot)", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_depot_solid_pickup.webp", "desc": "<p>This is the same as the other solid pickup station except it&#x27;s designed to work with the multi-station (&quot;depot&quot;) blueprints.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint book", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Trains Solid Dropoff (depot)", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_depot_solid_dropoff.webp", "desc": "<p>This is the same as the other solid dropoff station except it&#x27;s designed to work with the multi-station (&quot;depot&quot;) blueprints.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint book", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Trains Liquid Pickup (depot)", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_depot_liquid_pickup.webp", "desc": "<p>This is the same as the other liquid pickup station except it&#x27;s designed to work with the multi-station (&quot;depot&quot;) blueprints.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint book", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Magic Trains Liquid Dropoff (depot)", "category": "Magic Trains!", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_depot_liquid_dropoff.webp", "desc": "<p>This is the same as the other liquid dropoff station except it&#x27;s designed to work with the multi-station (&quot;depot&quot;) blueprints.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint book", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Train Stop", "category": "Train Stops", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_stop.webp", "desc": "<p>A train stop with one waiting area behind it and the ability to enter from and exit to either direction. Snaps to grid for super easy placement. You can place the stop down and then place one of the solid or liquid pickup or dropoff blueprints above right overtop of it. The only difference between the two versions of the blueprint are that one has the stop more to the left and the other more to the right.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Version 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Version 2", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Train Stop Depot", "category": "Train Stops", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_depot.webp", "desc": "<p>An infinitely-expandable set of stops (I call this a &quot;depot&quot; elsewhere in this page). Snaps to grid for super easy placement. The depot pickup and dropoff blueprints above fit directly over top of these stops. You can add as many expansions as you want.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Initial Depot", "string": ""}, {"label": "Expansion", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Smelting Station", "category": "Train Stops", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_smelting_station.webp", "desc": "<p>Because it&#x27;s easier than building it yourself!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Yellow belts", "string": ""}, {"label": "Red belts", "string": ""}, {"label": "Blue belts", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Straight Segment", "category": "Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_segment.webp", "desc": "<p>A simple tile-able train segment. Snaps to grid for super easy placement.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Single segment", "string": ""}, {"label": "Three segments", "string": ""}, {"label": "Five segments", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Turn Segment", "category": "Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_turn_segment.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes the trains go different ways. Choo choo.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "U-Turn Segment", "category": "Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_uturn_segment.webp", "desc": "<p>Sometimes a train is like, &quot;Meh, I don&#x27;t even want to go this way, I want to go the other way.&quot; So like, this like, does that. Like. (You don&#x27;t actually need this because all the stations have turn-arounds built in but whatevs, you do you.)</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Train 4-Way Intersection", "category": "Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/four_way_intersection.webp", "desc": "<p>Chain signals are used to keep things fairly efficient. Also, the intersection blueprints are designed such that if you tile them next to each other, trains will wait until they can go through the entirety of all intersections before entering the first one, which should help with deadlocks and such.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Train T Intersection", "category": "Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/t_intersection.webp", "desc": "<p>Here, your happy train-going residents can take a break to have some tea, maybe some biscuits--oh hold up it&#x27;s T not tea my bad.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Train Crossing", "category": "Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_crossing.webp", "desc": "<p>Why would you use this instead of the 4-way intersection? I dunno. Maybe you&#x27;re into hashtags or something. #train-crossing.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Straight-to-Diagonal Segment 1", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_straight_to_diagonal_1.webp", "desc": "<p>This can be used to go from a straight train segment to a diagonal one.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Straight-to-Diagonal Segment 2", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_straight_to_diagonal_2.webp", "desc": "<p>This can be used to go from a straight train segment to a diagonal one.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Train Y Intersection 1", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/y_intersection_1.webp", "desc": "<p>Like the T intersection except it goes between two diagonal segments and a straight segment.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Train Y Intersection 2", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/y_intersection_2.webp", "desc": "<p>Like the T intersection except it goes between two straight segments and a diagonal segment.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Diagonal Segment", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_diagonal_segment.webp", "desc": "<p>A simple, tile-able train segment that goes diagonally.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Single segment", "string": ""}, {"label": "Three segments:", "string": ""}, {"label": "Five segments:", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Diagonal Turn Segment", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_diagonal_turn_segment.webp", "desc": "<p>Diagonal trains need to turn, too.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Diagonal U-Turn Segment", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_diagonal_uturn_segment.webp", "desc": "<p>If a train going diagonally turns around, it&#x27;s still going diagonally. So the opposite of diagonal is diagonal! Who knew?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Diagonal Train 4-Way Intersection", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/diagonal_four_way_intersection.webp", "desc": "<p>Can we just take a moment to acknowledge how pretty this is? I mean, it&#x27;s pretty. Real pretty. I took great pains to make it so you could rotate it any way and it would still be the same (except for that power poll in the middle that will rotate around the roboport). But you probably didn&#x27;t even notice that, did you? I worked so hard on it! But you&#x27;ll never know! You probably aren&#x27;t even reading this! I&#x27;m talking to myself on the internet and it&#x27;s sad but also dang that intersection is pretty, amiright?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Diagonal Train 3-Way Intersection", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/diagonal_t_intersection.webp", "desc": "<p>For when you want an intersection but you have an irrational fear of even numbers like 4.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Diagonal Train Crossing", "category": "Diagonal Train Segments & Intersections", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/diagonal_crossing.webp", "desc": "<p>Don&#x27;t cross these trains! Oh wait. Do. Do cross these trains. It&#x27;s okay, the intersection will take care of it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Two-way Interchange", "category": "Train Two-Way Rails", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_two_way_interchange.webp", "desc": "<p>A one-way to two-way interchange. Two-way rails aren&#x27;t as efficient, but they _are_ cheaper and perform okay if you don&#x27;t have too many trains, making them an attractive option early-game.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Top Rail", "string": ""}, {"label": "Bottom Rail", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Train stop", "category": "Train Two-Way Rails", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_two_way_stop.webp", "desc": "<p>A train-stop for a two-way rail. Trains can only enter from one side but they can exit to either.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Version 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Version 2", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Two-way Rail Segment", "category": "Train Two-Way Rails", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_two_way_segment.webp", "desc": "<p>For trains that go both ways. Sorry. The joke was just, like, _right there_!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Two-way Rail Turn", "category": "Train Two-Way Rails", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_two_way_turn.webp", "desc": "<p>There are two versions of this so that whichever side the rail is on you can connect it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Top Rail", "string": ""}, {"label": "Bottom Rail", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Two-way Rail Turnaround", "category": "Train Two-Way Rails", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_two_way_turnaround.webp", "desc": "<p>Train around, it&#x27;s right behind you!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Top Rail", "string": ""}, {"label": "Bottom Rail", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Two-way Rail to Diagonal", "category": "Train Two-Way Rails", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_two_way_diagonal_interchange.webp", "desc": "<p>For all your diagonal interchange needs. I don&#x27;t think you have any of those needs. But if you do, this is for them.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Version 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Version 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Version 3", "string": ""}, {"label": "Version 4", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Two-way Rail Diagonal Segment", "category": "Train Two-Way Rails", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_two_way_diagonal_segment.webp", "desc": "<p>Is anyone reading this? Anyone at all?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Two-way Rail Diagonal Turn", "category": "Train Two-Way Rails", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_two_way_diagonal_turn.webp", "desc": "<p>It goes the direction that is 90 degrees different than the direction it was going before.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Top Rail", "string": ""}, {"label": "Bottom Rail", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Two-way Rail Diagonal Turnaround", "category": "Train Two-Way Rails", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/train_two_way_diagonal_turnaround.webp", "desc": "<p>For when it&#x27;s time to go home.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Top Rail", "string": ""}, {"label": "Bottom Rail", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Basic Stuff", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/basic_stuff.webp", "desc": "<p>A bunch of useful very early game things. I tried to have this more-or-less prioritize the things you&#x27;ll be most in need of. This includes some personal gears and green circuits which might be helpful as you manually create things.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Fast Inserters", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/fast_inserters.webp", "desc": "<p>This makes fast inserters. But does it make fast inserters fast? Or fast fast inserters? Or fast fast inserters fast? No, of course not, there are no fast fast inserters you n00b!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Assembling Machine 2s", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/assembling_machine_2.webp", "desc": "<p>You can have your assembling machine 2 in any color, as long as it&#x27;s blue.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Steel Poles and Furnaces", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/steel_poles_and_furnaces.webp", "desc": "<p>I steel got it!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Red Belts", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/red_belts.webp", "desc": "<p>I feel like I&#x27;m always hurting from red belts just after they are researched, so this is designed to produce them at a pretty decent pace.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Floors and Gates", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/floors_and_gates.webp", "desc": "<p>This makes refined concrete at a decent pace. I also threw in gates because you unlock them around this time and I don&#x27;t know where else to put them.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Trains!", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/trains.webp", "desc": "<p>Trains! For all your train-related needs. I also threw in a box to hold some personal engines in case you need them to build a car or tank or something.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Oil Stuff", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/oil_stuff.webp", "desc": "<p>This is everything you need to get basic oil running. It doesn&#x27;t produce pipes because my Basic Stuff blueprint does that already.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Bulk Inserters", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/bulk_inserters.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes bulk inserts in bulk. Or at least in normal. I mean, they stack in a chest so that kinda feels bulky. I dunno.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Circuit Stuff", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/circuit_stuff.webp", "desc": "<p>Imma be honest with you: there are whole sets of things in here I&#x27;ve never really used. I&#x27;ve played so much factorio and yet I still feel like a n00b.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Solar, Accumulators, and Substations", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/solar.webp", "desc": "<p>This produces solar panels and accumulators at about the ideal ratio. I also threw in substations because I find they&#x27;re very helpful when you&#x27;re doing solar.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Robots", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/robots.webp", "desc": "<p>This will produce logistics and construction robots at a decent pace and place them directly into a roboport. It also creates roboports, chests, and a few intermediates for personal use. It takes a little to get going, mostly because the chests production part gets a bit greedy, but nevertheless it produces pretty well.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Electric Furnaces", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/electric_furnaces.webp", "desc": "<p>I&#x27;m getting tired of writing these. Are you getting tired of reading these? This thing makes electric furnaces, okay? What else can I say? Why are you still reading this? Move on, man! Move on! Or ... woman. Move on, woman! Just, whoever you are, move on.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Assembling Machine 3s", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/assembling_machine_3.webp", "desc": "<p>I like this blueprint. It&#x27;s kinda symmetrical and pretty. It makes assembling machine 3s and consumes an entire yellow copper belt to make one every 12 seconds or so (assuming you are producing them with assembling machine 3s).</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Nuclear Items", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/nuclear_items.webp", "desc": "<p>This big ol&#x27; thing will produce everything you need to get nuclear up and running. It&#x27;s extremely resource hungry and still takes a while to output what you&#x27;ll need. But once you have nuclear going, it should eventually fill up and mostly sit idle.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Blue Belts", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/blue_belts.webp", "desc": "<p>For when you have the NEED for SPEED and also the THIRST YOU CAN&#x27;T SLATE to GOBBLE UP IRON PLATES!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Robochests", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/robochests.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes more roboty things.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Beacon of Hope", "category": "Base", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/beacons.webp", "desc": "<p>This is enough to keep one assembling machine continuously producing beacons. Is that enough? That&#x27;s probably enough. I dunno maybe you super late game people would scoff at it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Basic Military Stuff", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/basic_military_stuff.webp", "desc": "<p>Creates useful early military thingamabobs.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Military 2", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/military_2.webp", "desc": "<p>Grenades! Show those trees whose boss! Oh, I guess this also makes ammo for bugs, meh, whatever. Stupid trees.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Flamethrower Turrets and Ammo", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/flamethrower_turrets.webp", "desc": "<p>Listen, sometimes you just gotta burn stuff, like trees, or alien bugs that are just trying to defend their environmental paradise of a homeland from a smaug-producing psychopath who&#x27;s willing to wipe out their entire planet just to leave in a rocket, only to decide he doesn&#x27;t want to leave afterall because he&#x27;s having too much fun destroying their planet. I mean, what if the alien-equivalent of Captain Planet shows up? You gotta burn him, you know? You just gotta burn him.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Landmines Not Yours", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/landmines.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes the hidden booms.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Bust a Cap(sule)", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/capsules.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes capsules. You can bust &#x27;em.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Rockets", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/rockets.webp", "desc": "<p>I know what you&#x27;re thinking, because it&#x27;s the same thing I&#x27;m thinking. It&#x27;s the same thing we&#x27;re all thinking: EXPLOSIONS!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Explosive Rockets", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/explosive_rockets.webp", "desc": "<p>Slap this down on top of the Rockets blueprint to expand it or just put this down solo, either works.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Laser Turrets", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/laser_turrets.webp", "desc": "<p>Pew Pew</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Cannon Shells", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/cannon_shells.webp", "desc": "<p>Ammo for your lovely tank.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Military 4", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/military_4.webp", "desc": "<p>Cluster grenades and piercing shotgun shells.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "My-I-Mean-Ur-anium Ammo", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/uranium_ammo.webp", "desc": "<p>It&#x27;s neat how inexpensive this stuff is once you get uranium up and running.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Artillery", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/artillery.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes the biggest booms.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Defender Capsules", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/defender_capsules.webp", "desc": "<p>Robots don&#x27;t have souls, so remember that when you watch them plummet to the ground after their tiny little bit of life runs out.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Distractor Capsules", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/distractor_capsules.webp", "desc": "<p>Okay ... you remember before, when I said robots don&#x27;t have souls? Well that was technically a lie. Distractor robots do, in fact, have an experimental soul software installed. It doesn&#x27;t serve any purpose, though. The goal was simply to make them really feel the pain and loss of death when they are terminated after such a short time. It&#x27;s horrible, I know. But, whatcha gonna do, eh? Ha ha! Whatcha gonna do!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Destroyer Capsules", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/destroyer_capsules.webp", "desc": "<p>Destroyer capsules do not _have_ souls--they _take_ souls!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Module 1s", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/module_1.webp", "desc": "<p>This creates modules 1s at a good pace. To match my other blueprints, it creates more efficiency modules than anything else. But it&#x27;s easy to switch any of the assembling machines from any module type to any other type--they all have the same requirements.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Module 2s", "category": "Military", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/module_2.webp", "desc": "<p>Module 2s, baby!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Speed, Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Speed, Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}, {"label": "Efficiency, Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Efficiency, Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}, {"label": "Productivity, Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Productivity, Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Automation Science", "category": "Science", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/automation_science.webp", "desc": "<p>The first of the science blueprints. I designed these to be expandable, so each one builds on the last. They all produce science at the same rate.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Logistic Science", "category": "Science", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/logistic_science.webp", "desc": "<p>Science level 2 for you, boo! Okay, sorry. I crossed a line. You are not my boo. Rhyming is no excuse for calling you my boo.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Military Science", "category": "Science", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/military_science.webp", "desc": "<p>Science for the blowing up of things.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Chemical Science", "category": "Science", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/chemical_science.webp", "desc": "<p>Chemical science ... what is that exactly? Like chemistry? Why not call it chemistry?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Production Science", "category": "Science", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/production_science.webp", "desc": "<p>More science. I have nothing useful to say here.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Utility Science", "category": "Science", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/utility_science.webp", "desc": "<p>The final of the expandable blueprints! (Psst! You want to know a secret? This thing has too much low density structure production. They changed things in Space Age but I never updated it! I just left it not perfect! Do you know how hard that was for me? Do you know? DO YOU KNOW?!?)</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Assembling Machine 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Assembling Machine 3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Electronic Circuits", "category": "Intermediates", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/electronic_circuits.webp", "desc": "<p>You probably won&#x27;t need these since they&#x27;re baked into the other blueprints, but they&#x27;re here if you want &#x27;em!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "AM2 Yellow Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Yellow Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Red Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Red Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Blue Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Blue Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Yellow Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Yellow Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Red Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Red Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Blue Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Blue Belt In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Iron Gear Wheels", "category": "Intermediates", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/iron_gear_wheels.webp", "desc": "<p>You also likely won&#x27;t need these but they are here if you want them.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "AM2 Yellow Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Yellow Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Red Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Red Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Blue Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Blue Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Yellow Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Yellow Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Red Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Red Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Blue Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Blue Belt In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Plastic Bars", "category": "Intermediates", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/plastic_bars.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;ll never guess what these make!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Yellow Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "Yellow Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "Red Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "Red Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "Blue Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "Blue Belt In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Advanced Circuits", "category": "Intermediates", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/advanced_circuits.webp", "desc": "<p>Each of these will produce a half-yellow-belt of red circuits. They tend to be long, so if you want more red circuit production I suggest just slapping down more of these blueprints.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "AM2 Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Sulfuric Acid", "category": "Intermediates", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/sulfuric_acid.webp", "desc": "<p>Okay, unlike the other intermediate blueprints, this one you might actually want. It&#x27;s much easier to make this separately since you need to pipe it to miners for uranium.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Processing Unit", "category": "Intermediates", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/processing_units.webp", "desc": "<p>Each of these is designed to consume a full belt of green circuits.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "AM2 Yellow Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Yellow Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Red Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Red Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Blue Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 Blue Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Yellow Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Yellow Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Red Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Red Belt In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Blue Belt Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Blue Belt In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Explosives", "category": "Intermediates", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/explosives.webp", "desc": "<p>For when you need to make things to make other things make other things go boom.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Concrete", "category": "Intermediates", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/concrete.webp", "desc": "<p>So, let&#x27;s say you saw a beautiful field of soft grass and vibrant trees and thought, &quot;Yup, it&#x27;s gotta go.&quot; This does that!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Electric Engines", "category": "Intermediates", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/electric_engines.webp", "desc": "<p>Let me ask you a question. Why would a regular engine be required to make an electric engine? That&#x27;s weird, right? I mean, are the folks at Tesla like, &quot;Shoot, we can&#x27;t upgrade production because we need more gas-powered engines so we can break them down and then use the parts to create electric engines.&quot; I don&#x27;t get it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Tileable Defense Walls", "category": "Defense", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/defense_wall.webp", "desc": "<p>A whole bunch of defense blueprints. These fit with the robot extension and/or railroad segments. The double-rows of laser turrets should be good enough to handle just about any late-game threat, at least on Nauvis.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Straight, Turrets, Right Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Straight, Turrets, Left Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Straight, Turrets & Lasers, Right Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Straight, Turrets & Lasers, Left Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Straight, 1 Laser Row", "string": ""}, {"label": "Straight, 2 Laser Rows", "string": ""}, {"label": "Corner, Turrets, Right Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Corner, Turrets, Left Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Corner, Turrets & Lasers, Right Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Corner, Turrets & Lasers, Left Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Corner, 1 Laser Row", "string": ""}, {"label": "Corner, 2 Laser Rows", "string": ""}, {"label": "Edge, Turrets, Right Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Edge, Turrets, Left Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Edge, Turrets & Lasers, Right Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Edge, Turrets & Lasers, Left Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Edge, 1 Laser Row", "string": ""}, {"label": "Edge, 2 Laser Rows", "string": ""}, {"label": "Inside Corner, Turrets, Right Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Inside Corner, Turrets, Left Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Inside Corner, Turrets & Lasers, Right Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Inside Corner, Turrets & Lasers, Left Belt Direction", "string": ""}, {"label": "Inside Corner, 1 Laser Row", "string": ""}, {"label": "Inside Corner, 2 Laser Rows", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Late Game Beacon Wrapper", "category": "Late Game Beaconed Builds", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/beaconed_wrapper.webp", "desc": "<p>You can slap down a whole bunch of these together and then use the blueprints below to ramp up production of various items easily. The only downside is excessive power consumption, but hey, that&#x27;s what nuclear and fusion power is for, right?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Late Game Beaconed Builds", "category": "Late Game Beaconed Builds", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/beaconed_late_game.webp", "desc": "<p>A whole bunch of blueprints for scaling up production of various items. There will likely be items you want that are missing here, but it should be easy to use one of the existing blueprints as ... uh ... a blueprint ... for making anything you want.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Iron Gear Wheel", "string": ""}, {"label": "Copper Wire", "string": ""}, {"label": "Plastic", "string": ""}, {"label": "Green Circuit", "string": ""}, {"label": "Red Circuit", "string": ""}, {"label": "Blue Circuit", "string": ""}, {"label": "Speed Module 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Efficiency Module 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Productivity Module 1", "string": ""}, {"label": "Speed Module 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Efficiency Module 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Productivity Module 2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Beacon", "string": ""}, {"label": "Low Density Structure", "string": ""}, {"label": "Rocket Silo", "string": ""}, {"label": "Engine Unit", "string": ""}, {"label": "Electric Engine Unit", "string": ""}, {"label": "Pipe", "string": ""}, {"label": "Underground Pipe", "string": ""}, {"label": "Space Platform Starter Pack", "string": ""}, {"label": "Space Platform", "string": ""}, {"label": "Cargo Bay", "string": ""}, {"label": "Asteroid Collector", "string": ""}, {"label": "Crusher", "string": ""}, {"label": "Thruster", "string": ""}, {"label": "Rocket Launcher", "string": ""}, {"label": "Rocket Turret", "string": ""}, {"label": "Cargo Landing Pad", "string": ""}, {"label": "Lab", "string": ""}, {"label": "Cliff Explosives", "string": ""}, {"label": "Barrel", "string": ""}, {"label": "Grenade", "string": ""}, {"label": "Exposive", "string": ""}, {"label": "Sulfur", "string": ""}, {"label": "Automation Science", "string": ""}, {"label": "Logistic Science", "string": ""}, {"label": "Inserter", "string": ""}, {"label": "Transport Belt", "string": ""}, {"label": "Battery", "string": ""}, {"label": "Personal Battery", "string": ""}, {"label": "Personal Battery Mk2", "string": ""}, {"label": "Personal Battery Mk3", "string": ""}, {"label": "Heating Tower", "string": ""}, {"label": "Stone Furnace", "string": ""}, {"label": "Bioler", "string": ""}, {"label": "Heat Pipe", "string": ""}, {"label": "Artillery Turret", "string": ""}, {"label": "Artillery Shell", "string": ""}, {"label": "Radar", "string": ""}, {"label": "Solar Panel", "string": ""}, {"label": "Accumulator", "string": ""}, {"label": "Military Science", "string": ""}, {"label": "Piercing Rounds", "string": ""}, {"label": "Firearm Magazine", "string": ""}, {"label": "Wall", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Late Game Beaconed Foundry Builds", "category": "Late Game Beaconed Builds", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/beaconed_foundry_build.webp", "desc": "<p>Some useful blueprints for getting that sweet, sweet productivity bonus from foundries.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Iron Plate", "string": ""}, {"label": "Steel Plate", "string": ""}, {"label": "Iron Gear Wheel", "string": ""}, {"label": "Copper Plate", "string": ""}, {"label": "Copper Wire", "string": ""}, {"label": "Iron Stick", "string": ""}, {"label": "Low-Density Structure", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Space Foundation", "category": "Space", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/space_foundation.webp", "desc": "<p>These will make space foundation so you can leave that crummy-old planet and go ruin some others, too!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "AM2 Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM2 In-Out", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 Through", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3 In-Out", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Initial Rocket Silos", "category": "Space", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/rocket_silo_initial.webp", "desc": "<p>You can use this to create that initial space science platform and such, for manually launching rockets. I recommend upgrading to the one below at a certain point, since you&#x27;ll need a lot of rockets!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "AM2", "string": ""}, {"label": "AM3", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Rocket Silos", "category": "Space", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/rocket_silos.webp", "desc": "<p>You can tile these to create an area that can launch many rockets. I don&#x27;t recommend using it for your first rocket, but once you need to scale up this should do the trick!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Space Science", "category": "Space", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/space_science.webp", "desc": "<p>A nice, simple blueprint for getting space science. It&#x27;s fairly minimal and produces well. I really like this one! If you need to scale up, just create a few more.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Inner Planet Transport", "category": "Space", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/inner_planet_transport.webp", "desc": "<p>You can use this to travel between Nauvis, Vulcanus, Gleba, and Fulgora. Don&#x27;t try to go to Aquilo or beyond or you will have a bad day. This will slow itself down if it runs low on ammo, so you can mostly set it and forget it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Aquilo Transport", "category": "Space", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/aquilo_transport.webp", "desc": "<p>This will handle travel to the inner planets or Aquilo. It&#x27;s got some decent features: it will slow down when going to / from Aquilo if low on ammo, if you have excess space rocks it will recycle whichever one you have most of, and it has a decent amount of cargo space.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Edge & Beyond", "category": "Space", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/edge_and_beyond.webp", "desc": "<p>This will go out to the Solar System Edge and can go beyond it (at least, you know, a little). It&#x27;s not _great_ so you may have to babysit it some. It has features similar to the Aquilo Transport.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Solar Block", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/solar_block_vulcanus.webp", "desc": "<p>A solar block optimized for Vulcanus. Solar works pretty well on Vulcanus so it&#x27;s not a bad choice.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Simple Coal Liquefaction", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/simple_coal_liquefaction.webp", "desc": "<p>Use this to get oil products going on Vulcanus. You can upgrade to the normal Coal Liquefaction blueprint below once you&#x27;ve researched it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Coal Liquefaction (Vulcanus)", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/liquefaction_vulcanus.webp", "desc": "<p>Make that coal into oil products! This version is just like the Nauvis version but with minor modifications to work well on Vulcanus (like using sulfuric acid). You&#x27;ll need to kick start it with some heavy oil and some fuel in the biolers, but once you&#x27;ve done that it runs on it&#x27;s own.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Molten Iron", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/molten_iron.webp", "desc": "<p>I&#x27;m looking at this blueprint and, you know, there&#x27;s just something about it. Something like, mhm, yeah, you go blueprint. One could say it&#x27;s ... hot! The stone this produces will need to be handled, so that means either turning it into stone brick or just dumping it in lava (preferably both--send it to stone bricks until that backs up and then send the rest to the lava).</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Molten Copper", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/molten_copper.webp", "desc": "<p>*Sizzle* Still hot!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Low Density Structure (Vulcanus)", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/low_density_structure_vulcanus.webp", "desc": "<p>Helps to make those rockets so you can get off this hellscape!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Rocket Fuel (Vulcanus)", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/rocket_fuel_vulcanus.webp", "desc": "<p>Rockets are all like &quot;Zoom zoom pew pew&quot; and I like that, you know? I like that.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Processing Unit (Vulcanus)", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/blue_chips_vulcanus.webp", "desc": "<p>When the chips are down ... maybe just pick them back up? Then put them in a rocket. Then fly away. Just make sure they&#x27;re blue.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Metallurgical Science Pack", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/metallurgical_science.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes the Vulcanus science pack at a decent-ish rate.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Foundry", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/foundry.webp", "desc": "<p>This makes foundries! I like foundries. This assumes you are using robots. You should definitely be using robots.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Big Mining Drill", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/big_mining_drill.webp", "desc": "<p>When you want to show those ores who&#x27;s boss.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Tungsten Carbide", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/tungsten_carbide.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes tungsten carbide for off-world shipping.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Tungsten Plate", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/tungsten_plate.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes tungsten plate for off-world shipping (or on-world green belt production). The smaller blueprint (shown) only makes a few but the larger one produces quite a lot and you&#x27;ll probably want to use it if you plan to make green belts. Also, you should plan to make green belts.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Some", "string": ""}, {"label": "Lots", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Turbo Belts", "category": "Vulcanus", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/turbo_belts.webp", "desc": "<p>This makes those handy green belts! I definitely recommend producing them. Vulcanus can make them fairly easily and they are useful for late-game ships if for nothing else.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Small Power Block", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/power_block_fulgora_small.webp", "desc": "<p>This will harvest that lightning into power! I recommend doing something like this and scaling up as you can for power on fulgora as that seems to work best.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Big Power Block", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/power_block_fulgora.webp", "desc": "<p>Something this size is really nice for getting lots of power, but you may have trouble figuring out where to place it, so you might want to use the small one.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Steam Power", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/steam_power_fulgora.webp", "desc": "<p>As an alternate to lightning power, you can use this. It&#x27;s less resource-intensive and produces decent output so it might be the better option, but, hey, that&#x27;s up to you!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Storage Block", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/storage_block_fulgora.webp", "desc": "<p>My fulgora blueprints rely heavily on robots and on having enough logistics storage, so you&#x27;ll want 1 (or 2 or 3 or 4) of these for sure.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Recycling Line", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/recycling_line.webp", "desc": "<p>Takes in scrap, sends out precious, precious resources! This uses active provider chests to get rid of items quickly. The reprocessing center below will handle it from there!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Yellow Scrap Belt", "string": ""}, {"label": "Two Yellow Scrap Belts", "string": ""}, {"label": "Red Scrap Belt", "string": ""}, {"label": "Two Red Scrap Belts", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Reprocessing Center", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/reprocessing_center.webp", "desc": "<p>Uses circuits and robots to reprocess items, but only when needed! Circuits are used to only send items to reprocessing if you have too many of them. One of these is optmized to fully handle the output of the &quot;Two Red Scrap Belts&quot; Recyling Line blueprint (assuming no upgrades). This makes sure your resources don&#x27;t back up and stop all production but also makes sure you aren&#x27;t reprocessing things that you need!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Rocket Fuel (Fulgora) (Tileable)", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/rocket_fuel_fulgora.webp", "desc": "<p>A tileable rocket fuel blueprint. This is all you need to create stuff for rockets, since you pull blue chips and low density structures straight out of the ground. Man, I love Fulgora--don&#x27;t you love Fulgora? Stupid Gleba _wishes_ it was as cool as Fulgora.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Recyclers", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/recyclers.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes recyclers. &#x27;Nuff said. Well, I didn&#x27;t actually say &quot;&#x27;Nuff&quot; but pretend I did.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Holmium Plates", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/holmium_plates.webp", "desc": "<p>A little known fact: holmium plates were named for Sherlock Holms. Not Sherlock Holmes, that&#x27;s a totally different dude.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Electromagnetic Plants", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/electromagnetic_plants.webp", "desc": "<p>These aren&#x27;t anything like other plants, like the cactus or the fern.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Accumulators (Fulgora)", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/accumulators_fulgora.webp", "desc": "<p>I find it helpful to make these on-planet so you can easily expand your power capacity.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Lightning Rods", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/lightning_rods.webp", "desc": "<p>Makes lightning rods. Also contains a lightning rod. Which came first, the lightning rod machine or the lightning rod?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Substations (Fulgora)", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/substation_fulgora.webp", "desc": "<p>Like the accumulators, I find it helpful to build these on Fulgora to easily expand the power grid.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Superconductors", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/superconductors.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;ll need these both on- and off-planet.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Supercapacitors", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/supercapacitor.webp", "desc": "<p>Cuz regular capacitors are, like, so boring.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Electromagnetic Science Pack", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/electromagnetic_science.webp", "desc": "<p>Once you&#x27;ve built this, you&#x27;re just about there! You&#x27;ve beaten Fulgora! Congratulations! But, uh, don&#x27;t forget Tesla turrets. You know, if you want them. They might be a big help on Gleba. Frickin&#x27; Gleba.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Tesla Turrets", "category": "Fulgora", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/tesla_turrets.webp", "desc": "<p>These might be a good investment for Gleba defense. Their power usage is insane but so is their damage.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Solar Block (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/solar_block_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>Definitely don&#x27;t rely on solar on Gleba in the long run. But you may want something like this to kickstart everything. It&#x27;s ratios are optimized for Gleba.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Burner Power", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/power_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>This performs two very important roles: 1) it gives you power and 2) it disposes of materials you will want to get rid of. The initial blueprint will make sure to burn pentapod eggs, optionally burn rocket fuel when you&#x27;re low on heat, and burn other items if you have too many in logistics storage. The expander just adds more burning of materials if you have too many of them. The expander (rocket fuel) adds more rocket fuel burning if your normal resources aren&#x27;t enough to power things (I haven&#x27;t really needed to use this, though). I have found this to work pretty well for power on Gleba all on it&#x27;s own, once it gets going, and it can even support laser and tesla turrets and such.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Initial", "string": ""}, {"label": "Expander", "string": ""}, {"label": "Expander (Rocket Fuel)", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Harvesting", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/gleba_harvesting.webp", "desc": "<p>A simple harvesting blueprint for either Yumako or Jellynut. The requestor chest requests seeds.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Yumako", "string": ""}, {"label": "Jellynut", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Nutrients & Seeds", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/nutrients_and_seeds.webp", "desc": "<p>This produces nutrients for powering things and seeds for replanting. Like all my Gleba blueprints, it relies on robots. I find using robots to be _extremely helpful_ on Gleba. It keeps things simple and compact and Gleba seems to have no trouble powering this setup.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Agricultural Science", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/agricultural_science.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;ll need to kickstart this with a couple of pentapod eggs. In theory, this should never let a pentapod egg spoil and spawn a bug. I&#x27;ve also never seen it happen in practice so it seems pretty safe. Oh, yeah, also this creates science or something.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Iron Plate (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/iron_plates_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>This kick starts itself, isn&#x27;t wasteful, and ... and I just love it, okay? I&#x27;m really proud of it. Someone affirm me, already.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Copper Plate (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/copper_plates_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>I love this one, too! *Chef&#x27;s kiss*!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Steel Plate (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/steel_plate_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>Very simple (and kinda wasteful, power-wise) steel plate smelting.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Plastic Bar (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/plastic_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>Organic plastic, I guess? I don&#x27;t get it.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Electronic Circuits (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/electronic_circuit_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>Simple green circuit production.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Advanced Circuits (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/advanced_circuits_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>Red circuits or something I dunno I&#x27;m tired of writing these.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Landfill", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/landfill_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;ll definitely need plenty of this on Gleba. You can choose belt-fed or robot-fed.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Robot-Fed", "string": ""}, {"label": "Belt-Fed", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Biochamber", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/biochamber.webp", "desc": "<p>Biochamber production that should be safe from pentapod egg spoilage. You&#x27;ll have to kickstart it with a couple of pentapod eggs.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Rocket Fuel (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/rocket_fuel_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>Why can&#x27;t Gleba be more like Fulgora and make rocket fuel super easily?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Low Density Structure (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/low_density_structure_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>Why can&#x27;t Gleba be more like Fulgora and make low density structures super easily?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Processing Units (Gleba)", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/processing_unit_gleba.webp", "desc": "<p>Why can&#x27;t Gleba be more like Fulgora and make processing units super easily?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Carbon Fiber", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/carbon_fiber.webp", "desc": "<p>Carbon fiber for export to make cool things. Or, whatever you want. Send it to Vulcanus and then burn it in lava, what do I care?</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Stack Insert", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/stack_inserter.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;d think stack inserters would be really cool. But, actually, they&#x27;re total dorks. They&#x27;re always going on about their stamp collections and stuff. Geez, stack inserters. Get a life.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Death Hub", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/death_hub.webp", "desc": "<p>For killing the big bugs. This does a decent job but uses a LOT of power. But that&#x27;s what the &quot;Defense Support Array&quot; below is for! I don&#x27;t suggest using walls on Gleba cuz those dang monsters just walk over them.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Defense Support Array", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/defense_support_array.webp", "desc": "<p>One Death Hub can consume the power of two of these. So you might want a couple to make sure you can support spiky power usage if you are using the Death Hub above for defense.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Bioflux", "category": "Gleba", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/bioflux.webp", "desc": "<p>Bioflux for export.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Solar Kick Start (Aquilo)", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/solar_kickstart_aquilo.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;ll need something to kickstart the power on Aquilo. Just put a few of these down and then focus on getting the more useful power blocks below going--then you can remove these.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Power Starter (Aquilo)", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/nuclear_kickstart_aquilo.webp", "desc": "<p>This isn&#x27;t 100% necessary, but it will make life a whole lot easier. Heating towers take forever to get going. I&#x27;d suggest putting this down first and manually putting nuclear fuel in it. Once it gets going, robots will feed it but only if the heat gets too low (so you should need little or no fuel because the heating towers will take over).</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Fire & Ice Power", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/fire_and_ice_power.webp", "desc": "<p>It&#x27;s a bit tough to get the first one going, but once it starts these work well for providing power and heat. Just add more if you need more power. But be careful to do it slowly or you&#x27;ll suck all the heat away and your power will immediately die. This is tileable.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Ice Platform", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/ice_platform.webp", "desc": "<p>Produces ice platform and a little bit of heat. This is tileable with itself and the &quot;Fire &amp; Ice Power&quot; blueprint.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Cryogenic Plants", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/cryogenic_plant.webp", "desc": "<p>This will produce cryogenic plants. I am out of silly or clever things to say.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Fluoroketone", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/fluoroketone.webp", "desc": "<p>This make fluro--uh, I mean flouro--uh, I mean fluoru--Look! Nobody sane can spell this the first time! Anyway, whatever it makes, it makes it good. And it&#x27;s smart enough to shut down production and not over fill the tanks, so you should always have plenty of this but never backup the cryogenic plants that are cooling the liquid.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Cryogenic Science", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/cryogenic_science.webp", "desc": "<p>Aquilo science. Cool! (Get it?)</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Quantum Processor", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/quantum_processor.webp", "desc": "<p>Apparently, all we need on earth to finally get quantum computing out of it&#x27;s infancy is some place really, really cold. If it works in Factorio, it must be true!</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Fusion Fusion", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/fusion.webp", "desc": "<p>A fusion of fusion-based power items.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Railgun Turret", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/railgun_turret.webp", "desc": "<p>The only way to advance beyond the limits of your reach into space: Even. Bigger. Guns.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Fluoroketone Cold Barrel", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/fluoroketone_barrels.webp", "desc": "<p>You&#x27;ll need at least a little of this stuff for kickstarting fusion power on the &quot;Edge and Beyond&quot; ship or on other planets, so here&#x27;s a little blueprint for ya! It won&#x27;t make too many.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}, {"title": "Rocket Silo", "category": "Aquilo", "image": "https://autosaved-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/dev/images/factorio/blueprintsv3/rocket_silo_aquilo.webp", "desc": "<p>A tileable rocket silo blueprint for Aquilo.</p>", "blueprints": [{"label": "Blueprint", "string": ""}]}];
